#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# arg

#% text
# `arg(z)` gives the principal argument of the complex number `z`, the angle in `(-pi, pi]`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Exact arguments give exact angles: 0 for positive reals, `pi` for negative reals, `atan` forms otherwise. `arg(0)` is 0.

#% item
# `arg` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
arg(1 + im)
#% output
#= (1/4)*pi

#% cell
arg(-2)
#% output
#= pi

#% cell
arg(3 - 4*im)
#% output
#= -atan(4/3)

#% cell
arg(-1.0 - 1.0*im)
#% output
#= -2.356194490192345

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The polar form:

#% cell
z = -3 + 4*im; n(abs(z)*exp(im*arg(z)))
#% output
#= -2.999999999999999 + 4.000000000000001im

#% text
# The argument of a product is the sum, modulo `2*pi`:

#% cell
n(arg((1 + im)*(1 + 2*im)) - arg(1 + im) - arg(1 + 2*im))
#% output
#= 0.0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `abs`, `re`, `im_part`, `atan`
